opencourseware is a web-based program  that will provide free access to primary  materials for virtually every course at  mit the founders of ocw had a  transformative vision 20 years ago of  offering access  to  materials from the mit classroom openly  freely  they can learn from them straight off  the website they can download them and  carry them around they can remix them  with other kinds of materials and mash  them up in new ways they can share them  with their networks  we're getting about 22 million visits  per year we have more than 3 million  subscribers to the ocw youtube channel  it makes it the  biggest.edu youtube channel in the world  it has captured  curious learners of all stripes from  around the world  several thousand mit faculty have shared  materials from more than 2 500 courses  we're sharing materials not just from  the science technology engineering and  math courses and the management courses  that mit is most famous for but also  from the incredible richness of our  humanities and social sciences  the impact of ocw and opening learning  for millions around the world is  multiplied by the role of educators  elsewhere when they take materials from  ocw and repurpose them and use them and  make them part of their own teaching for  each one educator that does that there's  dozens or hundreds more people for whom  the opportunities to learn are opened up  it takes resources to do what we do at  opencourseware takes a lot of people and  time and energy and money  to cover the full curriculum at mit  we're right in the middle of launching  the program for ocw's third decade  we're delighted that we have now rolled  out its next generation platform it's  mobile friendly it has much better  search tools  what we teach at mit changes with time  how we teach changes with time and now  we have the new platform that will allow  us to keep the content of ocw current  and vibrant into the future  now it should be free and especially  knowledge that comes from leading  institutions institutions with the most  privilege behind them to give that back  to the world has never been more  important than it is today  so many of the challenges that the world  is facing require the development the  application the testing the refinement  of new forms of knowledge  we firmly believe that a world in which  the educational attainment of millions  of people has been elevated will be a  better world  this is making a difference  [Music]  you
 

